| D | `feat/ide-help` | U23–U26: help, onboarding, accessibility |
| E | `fix/ide-validation` | U27–U28: replay tests, persona panel, fixes |

**Run cycle:** same lean cycle as queue 1 (plan → build → validate). Phase A first and on its own (it's the base everything else builds on). Phases B and C can then run in two parallel lanes in worktrees (B owns `page/`, `doc.rs`, `mpp-syntax/document`; C owns `editor/`, `insert/`), with D after both. Fixers start on Sonnet and move to Opus from the 2nd attempt.

**Smooth typing target (Ben, 2026-11-21: "smooth out typing and cursor placement"):** Phase A isn't done until, in the U27 replay tests: (1) every key shows its character in the **same frame** it is pressed (under 16 ms on a debug build of a 200-line file); (2) the caret is drawn on the line and at the x where the next character will go, **on every frame**, including while answers are arriving; (3) no line on screen moves up or down while the user is typing on a different line; (4) clicking anywhere in text puts the caret exactly at the nearest character gap, and clicking in a maths box puts it in the nearest box slot. U2, U3, U9, U10, U15 and U19 all answer to this target.

**Testing rule for this whole queue (new):** every typing or cursor fix gets a test that **drives the real app the way a person does**: `egui_kittest` key and text events, through the **real frame loop including `pump()`**, not `settle()`. Queue 1's tests used `settle()` and so missed the missing-repaint bug. Screenshots under `target/ide-snapshots` must now be **compared** against stored images (with a small tolerance), not just written.

