### Design rules (from the survey; every item below follows these)
1. **Maths never looks like prose.** Maths has a light tint and a margin marker, and the caret changes colour inside it. Font alone is never the signal (Mathcha, Word math zones, LyX boxes). https://www.mathcha.io/documentation/components/basic-editing/ · https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/archive/blogs/murrays/when-formula-autobuildup-occurs
2. **The structure holding the caret is boxed** (fraction, root, exponent), with a fainter box for its parent, in a colour unlike the selection (TeXmacs focus boxes, Word). https://texmacs.org/tmdoc/main/editing/man-structured-move.en.html
3. **Shorthand converts only on a delimiter:** Space, an operator, a closing bracket, Enter or leaving the line, never on a timer mid-word. **The first Ctrl+Z gives back exactly what you typed** (MathLive, Word build-up). https://mathlive.io/mathfield/guides/shortcuts/
4. **One way out of everything:** Tab = next box, then out; Right at the end of a box = one level out; Space or an operator after `x^2` = out of the exponent; **Esc = leave maths into prose**; Enter = new line (MathLive, MathQuill, LyX). https://mathlive.io/mathfield/reference/keybindings/ · https://docs.mathquill.com/en/latest/Config/
5. **Re-rendering never moves the caret or the text.** Answers go in a space that is reserved before they arrive. Old answers stay, dimmed, until new ones land (Observable). Errors go in the same slot, never as extra lines. https://talk.observablehq.com/t/showing-cell-evaluation-progress/8000
6. **Speed:** react to a key within 0.1 s; show answers within ~1 s of the last key; show "working" only after 1 s (NN/g limits). https://www.nngroup.com/articles/response-times-3-important-limits/
7. **Accept linear typing and convert it**, rather than forcing templates. Studies found people are faster typing `a/b` than filling boxes (MathTOUCH). https://journals.gre.ac.uk/index.php/msor/article/view/415/pdf
8. **Typography:** single-letter variables italic; functions (sin, log), units and numbers upright (NIST SP 811); scripts 0.71× per level, never under ~9 px; extra line height on maths lines so scripts don't shift lines; colours pass WCAG 4.5:1 (text) and 3:1 (markers) in light and dark mode; state is never shown by colour alone. https://physics.nist.gov/cuu/pdf/typefaces.pdf · https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/contrast-minimum.html
9. **Always say where you are:** the status bar shows the mode (Prose / Maths) and the path to the caret ("Maths › fraction › denominator").

