| U19 | One way out of every structure | Implement rule 4 everywhere, in every template (`editor/template.rs`, `insert/mod.rs:366-412`): Tab / Shift+Tab = next / previous empty box, then out; Right at the end of a box = one level out, Left at the start = one level out to the left; typing `+ − = < > ,` or Space at the end of an exponent or subscript leaves it (`x^2+` → x²+, MathQuill `charsThatBreakOutOfSupSub`); `/` makes a fraction from the operand before it (already there) and Right/Tab moves numerator → denominator → out; Esc leaves maths and puts the caret in prose straight after it; Enter on a maths line = new maths line below. `x^^2` and similar slips are refused (MathQuill `supSubsRequireOperand`). | Opus | done (lane C1, ef255ac; PR #14) |
| U20 | Brackets that help, not fight | Typing `(` shows a faint ghost `)`, and typing `)` fills it in instead of adding a second one. Ghost brackets you didn't type are never saved. Backspace right after `(` removes both. Matching bracket highlights when the caret is next to one. Same for `[ ]`, `{ }`, `| |` (absolute value) and `\left( \right)`. | Sonnet | done (lane C2, 109cff9; PR #14). Brackets wait for the conversions (merge 0934cbe). |
